From: GPU lane (diagnosis 2026-11-21); rebased by CarPlay lane 2026-11-21
Subject: 0504 sweet_ufs pl_thread: make pandora_reboot_after independent of the log file

The bounded reset used to be checked after pl_flush(), and one failed UFS write
returned from the logging thread entirely, silently cancelling the reset for the
rest of the boot: the phone stays in iOS with USB enumerated until it is reset by
hand.  Check the deadline first, and keep the thread (and the deadline) alive after
logging stops.

Rebase note (CarPlay lane, 2026-11-21): the original 0504 was written against the
pre-0481 body, which ended the deadline branch with pl_psci_reset().  The tree now
uses the orderly shutdown path (reboot_kernel(RB_AUTOBOOT, NULL) with the
process-stop/sync/unmount drain), so that patch no longer applies -- `git apply`
fails at bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c:2219 against the buildtree that CI run 44800513767
actually compiled.  This version is the same intent expressed on the current body:
the deadline block moves above the lock and the flush, `!pl_ready` continues the
loop so the deadline keeps firing, and a write failure only clears pl_ready instead
of returning.  The orderly-shutdown branch is preserved verbatim.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
index 5fe98eb..d3eaa26 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c
@@ -2208,4 +2208,28 @@ pl_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
 	for (;;) {
 		(void)tsleep(&pl_chan, PZERO, "pandoralog", hz * (int)secs);
+		/*
+		 * 0504: the bounded reset must not be hostage to the log file. The deadline
+		 * used to be checked after pl_flush(), and a single failed write returned from
+		 * this thread entirely -- which silently cancelled pandora_reboot_after for the
+		 * rest of the boot and left the phone sitting in iOS with USB enumerated until
+		 * somebody reset it by hand.  Check the deadline before touching the disk; when
+		 * logging has already stopped, keep waking up and keep honouring the deadline.
+		 */
+		if (limit && mach_absolute_time() - start >= limit) {
+			printf("PANDORA: pandora_reboot_after=%u reached, shutting down cleanly\n", reboot_after);
+			/* A bounded trial is a normal shutdown, not a panic. Non-journaled HFS
+			 * bitmap buffers use delayed writes: resetting here can persist catalog
+			 * extents without their allocation bits and let the next boot reuse live data.
+			 * Use the existing process-stop/sync/unmount/buffer-drain path without the
+			 * UFS lock held. Its final PE_halt_restart still drains the console and resets.
+			 * Never fall back to an unsynced reset if another shutdown owns the system. */
+			int shutdown_error = reboot_kernel(RB_AUTOBOOT, NULL);
+			printf("PANDORA: orderly timed shutdown returned %d; no forced reset\n", shutdown_error);
+			limit = 0; /* do not repeat a shutdown request; retain console evidence */
+		}
+		if (!pl_ready) {
+			/* Logging failed earlier; sleep again so the deadline above still fires. */
+			continue;
+		}
 		lck_mtx_lock(&sweet_ufs_lock);
 		uint64_t now = mach_absolute_time();
@@ -2224,18 +2248,7 @@ pl_thread(__unused void *arg, __unused wait_result_t wr)
 		if (error) {
 			printf("PANDORA LOG: write failed (%d), log stopped\n", error);
+			/* Stop logging, but keep the thread alive: the deadline at the top of this
+			 * loop is what guarantees the phone comes back. Returning here stranded it. */
 			pl_ready = false;
-			return;
-		}
-		if (limit && mach_absolute_time() - start >= limit) {
-			printf("PANDORA: pandora_reboot_after=%u reached, shutting down cleanly\n", reboot_after);
-			/* A bounded trial is a normal shutdown, not a panic. Non-journaled HFS
-			 * bitmap buffers use delayed writes: resetting here can persist catalog
-			 * extents without their allocation bits and let the next boot reuse live data.
-			 * Use the existing process-stop/sync/unmount/buffer-drain path without the
-			 * UFS lock held. Its final PE_halt_restart still drains the console and resets.
-			 * Never fall back to an unsynced reset if another shutdown owns the system. */
-			int shutdown_error = reboot_kernel(RB_AUTOBOOT, NULL);
-			printf("PANDORA: orderly timed shutdown returned %d; no forced reset\n", shutdown_error);
-			limit = 0; /* do not repeat a shutdown request; retain console evidence */
 		}
 	}
